	&lt;div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			1) Rid premises of mice All required actions have been completed. &amp;bull; The cellar has been swept, cleared, disinfected and deep-cleaned. &amp;bull; All mouse droppings and contaminated items have been removed. &amp;bull; All surfaces, equipment, drinks, and food packaging have been externally cleaned. &amp;bull; All cardboard, damaged goods and opened disposables have been discarded. &amp;bull; Holes and entry points have been identified and sealed. &amp;bull; A pest-proofing survey has been completed. &amp;bull; A professional pest control contractor has been instructed for ongoing scheduled visits.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			2) Bar hand-wash basin - Basin is now fully clear, available and in permanent use. &amp;bull; Hot and suitably mixed water has been restored. &amp;bull; Boiler repair was completed and is fully operational.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			3) Coffee machine leak - The machine has been repaired and is now working with no leaks.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			4) Deep clean of bar floor - Full deep clean completed &amp;bull; All dirt, debris and broken glass removed.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			5) Repair wall&amp;ndash;floor junction - The peeling white joining strip has been repaired and refitted.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			6) Remove cardboard - All accumulated cardboard has been removed from the bar and cellar.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			7) Replace damaged rubber mats - All worn or damaged rubber mats have been replaced with new ones.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			8) Repair the cellar &amp;ndash; structural - The cellar walls, floors and ceiling have been painted and treated. &amp;bull; Mould removed, poor surfaces repaired, brickwork sealed, dust removed. &amp;bull; Condition is now clean, dry and fully fit for purpose.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			9) Clean cellar shelving - All shelving has been thoroughly cleaned and disinfected.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			10) Clean post-mix machine - Completed.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			11) Clean glass-storage shelving - Shelving and matting have been cleaned and sanitised.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			12) Remove expired foods - All expired items discarded. - A new stock-rotation and date-checking procedure is now in place.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			13) Replace damaged chopping board - Wooden engraved board has been removed and replaced with a food-safe board.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			14) Chemical contact times - Staff instructed and retrained on correct Jantex 30-second contact time. &amp;bull; Now included in daily checks. FSMS / Confidence in Management&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
			15) Full Food Safety Management System We have now implemented: &amp;bull; A complete FSMS based on Safer Food Better Business. &amp;bull; Daily recorded checks: fridge/freezer temperatures, opening/closing checks, pest checks, structural checks. &amp;bull; Clearly labelled durability dates for all open foods and drinks. &amp;bull; Legible dating on all perishables. &amp;bull; Correct manufacturer shelf-life applied. &amp;bull; A standalone written procedure for fruit dehydration. &amp;bull; A pest-management process integrated into daily recording.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;
